            title: 'Pip-Pip',
            subtitle: 'Marriage Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Pip-Pip is an English Marriage game for 4-10 players. Each marriage sets a new trump (like 1000, Marjapussi). Two packs (104 cards). 7 cards each; draw after each trick. Point values: 2=11, A=10, K/Q/J=5/4/3. All marriages score 50.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '20th-century British card books. Marriage family. Continental influence (1000, Marjapussi).',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four to ten players. Described in 20th-century British card game books; the game accommodates a larger group by using two packs; play is individual (no partnerships).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two standard packs shuffled together (104 cards).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '104 cards.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '7 each. Draw after each trick until stock exhausted.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
